The MTK overlay host tools are built from source by scripts/dtc/Makefile.
They are separate from the kernel's original dtc program and from loadable
target kernel modules. No precompiled dtc_overlay or ufdt_apply_overlay is
stored in this tree.

Source provenance
-----------------

scripts/dtc/aosp/dtc contains the required source subset from the AOSP-derived
LineageOS external/dtc repository:
  https://github.com/LineageOS/android_external_dtc
  0a190a66e1d414b546e053f844854d27fe3f3bd9

scripts/dtc/aosp/libufdt contains the required source subset from:
  https://github.com/LineageOS/android_system_libufdt
  c54fd0834ab980033cedd9441e83674e8a984d5f

aosp/UPSTREAM.json records the SHA-256 of every imported upstream file before
the local changes below. The import was read from those pinned Git objects,
not from mutable working-copy files. GPL/NOTICE/README.license and the license
markers are retained. DTC uses its GPL license. libufdt uses Apache 2.0 and
links the separately dual-licensed libfdt under its permissive BSD terms;
all original per-file copyright and license notices remain present.

Local source changes from those hashes are limited to:
  aosp/dtc/dtc-lexer.l:
    Declare the parser-owned yylloc as extern, avoiding a duplicate definition
    with host compilers that default to -fno-common.
  aosp/dtc/treesource.c:
    Remove an extra blank line at end of file; no code change.
  aosp/libufdt/tests/src/ufdt_overlay_test_app.c:
    Return a reported error when overlay application returns NULL instead of
    dereferencing NULL while writing the output.
  aosp/libufdt/tests/src/util.c:
    Reject failed seeks/nonpositive input lengths, and report partial writes
    or fclose() errors rather than claiming a successful output.

Build integration
-----------------

The normal kernel scripts target builds both programs using HOSTCC and
HOSTLDFLAGS. Generated lex/yacc C and headers stay under objtree. No host dtc,
fdtoverlay, libfdt, libufdt, or alternate prebuilt executable is selected.

scripts/Makefile.lib invokes:
  $(objtree)/scripts/dtc/dtc_overlay -@ -H both ...
and lists that executable as an explicit prerequisite of each DTB.
scripts/drvgen/drvgen.mk invokes:
  $(objtree)/scripts/dtc/ufdt_apply_overlay BASE OVERLAY OUTPUT
after scripts and the DTBs have built. The merge loop stops at its first
failure so a later successful overlay cannot hide an earlier error.

The explicit -H both is required for compatibility. The old binary reported
DTC 1.4.2-Android-build and emitted both phandle and linux,phandle. The pinned
source reports DTC 1.4.4-Android-build and defaults to ePAPR-only phandle.
Without -H both it removes 148 linux,phandle properties from mt6755.dtb and
93 from the K50 overlay. With -H both the current target outputs are byte-for-
byte identical, including symbols, fixups, property order, and padding.

Standalone kernel builds require flex and bison, or explicit HOSTLEX and
HOSTYACC overrides. The Android build's restricted PATH does not allow the
host flex/bison commands. Pass the existing Android toolchain paths explicitly
through the kernel make flags, using absolute paths to the Android tree:
  HOSTLEX=/absolute/android/prebuilts/build-tools/linux-x86/bin/flex
  HOSTYACC=/absolute/android/prebuilts/build-tools/linux-x86/bin/bison
  BISON_PKGDATADIR=/absolute/android/prebuilts/build-tools/common/bison

The bundled Android Flex 2.6.4 and Bison 2.7 were verified. System Flex 2.6.4
and Bison 3.8.2 were also verified. The Bison data path is part of the recorded
generation command, so changing it invalidates the generated outputs.

Verification for k50sv1_64_bsp
----------------------------

The bounded integration check used a fresh separate kernel output directory,
the actual build-2 .config, its Clang 8 host compiler/GCC 4.9 target compiler,
and the same explicit Python 2.7 DCT interpreter. olddefconfig, scripts, and
dtbs completed. The generated pin configuration and both DTS files were built
through the real Kbuild path. No full Android build or phone operation was
part of this check.

All three outputs match the preserved build-2 files and old tools exactly:
  mt6755.dtb              68590 bytes
    7238ba93ab8d56d282be216195720d558023ce601b76bb99e23cf1c82ac92fdd
  k50sv1_64_bsp.dtb       34627 bytes
    ec5cf27cd38358212890f2917040d6a31216c9b27b598de35f9428ddb0d411c1
  k50sv1_64_bsp.dtb.merge 103217 bytes
    cf70ef55b484bb38969bf68011ed1bcfda6993751d47080ca3f48db32b568ae3

compare-overlay-tools.py accepts explicit old/new executable paths, a preserved
kernel output directory containing those DTBs and their preprocessed
.NAME.dtb.dts.tmp files, and a directory for its evidence:

  python3 scripts/dtc/compare-overlay-tools.py \
    --old-dtc /preserved/dtc_overlay \
    --old-ufdt /preserved/ufdt_apply_overlay \
    --new-dtc /kernel-output/scripts/dtc/dtc_overlay \
    --new-ufdt /kernel-output/scripts/dtc/ufdt_apply_overlay \
    --baseline-output /preserved/kernel-output \
    --output /comparison-evidence

Its 22 checks cover both compilers, all four old/new merger/input pairings,
CLI errors, missing/malformed input, unwritable output, an unresolved overlay
symbol, and a delayed write failure. Nine ordinary error cases preserve the
old nonzero exit code. Two error-path improvements are intentional:
  unresolved symbol: old process died with SIGSEGV; new process returns 1;
  small output to /dev/full: old process returned 0; new process returns 1.

Kbuild dependency checks also confirmed that an unchanged invocation does not
recompile/relink either tool or regenerate either DTB, changing DTC source
rebuilds the compiler and both DTBs, changing UFDT source rebuilds only that
tool and the merged output, and deleting the generated parser files causes
them to be regenerated. Each case retained identical final content. A two-
overlay make harness using the real drvgen.mk confirmed that failure of the
first overlay returns failure and prevents the later overlay from running.

Other tracked host binaries
--------------------------

scripts/mkimage remains a legacy MediaTek image/header tool. No tracked kernel
rule invokes that path. The optional MTK_HEADER_SUPPORT=yes branch in the
legacy Android.mk names $(HOST_OUT_EXECUTABLES)/mkimage, while the generic
U-Boot uImage rules use scripts/mkuboot.sh and a different tool interface.
The active Lineage device build selects Image.gz through its kernel.mk and
does not invoke the tracked scripts/mkimage. Matching source for this legacy
binary was not found in the available tree. AOSP external/u-boot/tools/mkimage.c
is a different tool/interface and was not substituted.

tools/dct/old_dct/DrvGen and DrvGen.exe remain legacy assets. DrvGen.py invokes
the Linux binary only when its DWS input cannot be parsed as XML. The active
CONFIG_ARCH_MTK_PROJECT=k50sv1_64_bsp input is valid XML, so the source Python
generator handles it and the old binary is not executed. Other preserved DWS
files, including k50v1_64_bsp.dws, use the old format; matching old generator
source was not found. The Windows PE is not called by the kernel build.
These inactive binaries were retained rather than removed from unsupported
legacy configurations. The tracked host ELF count therefore falls from four
to two, and the legacy PE remains. This is not a claim that all BSP binaries
or all alternate board configurations have been replaced or validated.
